- decided_at: '2026-09-08T01:10:00+00:00'
  event: initial
  value: 'Read the route/output channel as an AUDITABILITY channel: the sender is the reasoner''s own nondeterministic resolution choice, the receiver is an auditor reading the surviving conclusions, and capacity bounds how much of the internal reasoning is recoverable from observed output. Do not read it as data transmission, and do not posit an intentional sender.'
  reason: 'This is the only framing under which the results already proved are the headline rather than scaffolding: zero-error capacity 0 becomes ''no observer can ever be certain which resolution was applied'', and the converse completes it. It requires no intent, no adversary model and no engineer, and it matches the limitative rhetorical mode of every other section. It also supports ''pointless'' directly: the machinery makes distinctions that do not survive into what it outputs. The side-channel reading was rejected because a leak is a harm and cuts against the title, and because it needs an observation model the paper does not have; the purely descriptive reading was rejected because it forfeits the word capacity.'
